{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Week 6, Day 2\n",
    "\n",
    "Before proceeding with our own MCP Server, let's just look at 2 popular marketplaces for what's out there:\n",
    "\n",
    "https://glama.ai/mcp  \n",
    "https://smithery.ai/servers \n",
    "\n",
    "We're about to create and use our own MCP Server!\n",
    "\n",
    "It's pretty simple, but it's not super-simple. The excitement around MCP is about how easy it is to share and use other MCP Servers - making our own does involve a bit of work.\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's review some python code made mostly by a hard-working Engineering Team:\n",
    "\n",
    "backend/accounts.py"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "False"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 17,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "from openai import OpenAI, AsyncOpenAI\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "from openai.types.responses import ResponseTextDeltaEvent\n",
    "import asyncio\n",
    "from typing import Dict\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
    "from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n",
    "from agents import Agent, Runner, trace, function_tool, SQLiteSession, OpenAIChatCompletionsModel\n",
    "from agents import GuardrailFunctionOutput, output_guardrail\n",
    "\n",
    "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "from openai import OpenAI, AsyncOpenAI\n",
    "from agents import Agent, Runner, trace\n",
    "from agents.mcp import MCPServerStdio\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
    "\n",
    "load_dotenv(override=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "GEMINI_BASE_URL = \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/\"\n",
    "google_api_key = os.getenv(\"Gemini_API\")\n",
    "\n",
    "gemini_client = AsyncOpenAI(base_url = GEMINI_BASE_URL, api_key=google_api_key)\n",
    "gemini_model = OpenAIChatCompletionsModel(model=\"gemini-3.5-flash-lite\", openai_client=gemini_client)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# On Windows, a stdio MCP server started from a Jupyter kernel writes to a stderr stream with no\n",
    "# real file descriptor and crashes with io.UnsupportedOperation: fileno. We send the server's\n",
    "# stderr to the null device so it always has somewhere real to write, which lets every cell below\n",
    "# use MCPServerStdio exactly as the OpenAI Agents SDK documents it. Mac and Linux are unaffected.\n",
    "import functools\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import agents.mcp.server\n",
    "\n",
    "agents.mcp.server.stdio_client = functools.partial(agents.mcp.server.stdio_client, errlog=subprocess.DEVNULL)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "sys.path.append(r\"c:\\training projects\")\n",
    "\n",
    "from backend.accounts import Account"
   ]
